        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Intended for use as a garment, clothing. Register description describes object as being 'worn by nobility' in their youth."@en , "Textile, trousers, purple green satin, applied gold and silver ribbon, Bhopal, ca. 1867"@en , "Wide-legged trousers of green brocaded silk with purple bands at waist and hem, with applied  decoration of embossed and twisted silver and gold ribbon and tinsel fringes. Cotton fabric lining waistband, appears to be of European origin."@en ;
